{"text": "Slovak 'two' changes with the gender of the noun: use 'dva' for masculine things and animals (dva stoly, dva psy), 'dve' for feminine and neuter nouns (dve ženy, dve okná), and 'dvaja' only for masculine people (dvaja muži, dvaja študenti). If a group of people is mixed or all female, use 'dve' or 'dvaja' by the usual rule for the noun, but at A1 just remember: dvaja = two guys, dve = women and neuter things, dva = everything else masculine."}

